**Given:**

Evaluate dfrac{9 sin θ + 2 cos θ}{9 sin θ - 2 cos θ}, if 3tan θ = 4.

**Formula used:**

tan θ = dfrac{sin θ}{cos θ}

**Calculation:**

3tan θ = 4

⇒ tan θ = dfrac{4}{3}

⇒ sin θ = dfrac{4k}{5} and cos θ = dfrac{3k}{5} (using k as a common multiple)

Substitute these values in the given expression:

dfrac{9 sin θ + 2 cos θ}{9 sin θ - 2 cos θ}

⇒ dfrac{9 (dfrac{4k}{5}) + 2 (dfrac{3k}{5})}{9 (dfrac{4k}{5}) - 2 (dfrac{3k}{5})}

⇒ dfrac{dfrac{36k}{5} + dfrac{6k}{5}}{dfrac{36k}{5} - dfrac{6k}{5}}

⇒ dfrac{dfrac{42k}{5}}{dfrac{30k}{5}}

⇒ dfrac{42k}{30k}

⇒ dfrac{42}{30}

⇒ dfrac{7}{5}

**∴ The correct answer is option (3).**

